WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.330
​​Supergirl​ is getting a new look for
season 5 - and it's as much a matter of practicality

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:06.900
than it is of fashion.

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:12.500
The new look was unveiled to fans as San Diego
Comic-Con, and the series' star Melissa Benoist

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:16.620
had a hilarious explanation for fans: she's
tired of freezing her legs off.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:21.540
Supergirl, AKA Kara Danvers, has undergone
a few slight tweaks to her wardrobe during

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:26.470
the show's run, most notably during season
4's climactic battle with Jon Cryer's Lex

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:27.599
Luthor and the Red Daughter.

00:00:27.599 --> 00:00:32.369
That costume switch may have been born of
necessity, but Kara's new look seems to be

00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:37.410
more of a direct fashion statement, an evolution
of her classic costume that aligns a little

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:40.800
more closely with the aesthetic of her famous
cousin, Superman.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:41.840
The biggest difference?

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:42.440
"Pants!

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:43.760
Pants!

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:44.620
Pants!

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.000
Pants!"

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:51.100
According to Benoist, she and the series'
producers simply figured that it was time

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:52.140
for a little update.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:55.760
But, as Benoist told Entertainment Tonight,
there was another reason for the switch, as

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:56.260
well.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:01.219
That reason has to do with the fact that Supergirl
shoots primarily in Vancouver, Canada, and

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:02.940
often in the dead of winter.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:09.000
"Then we moved to Vancouver and it was cold
and it rained, and it feels right, it feels

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.200
like the right evolution and the right time
to do it."

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:17.340
Although Benoist has acquitted herself spectacularly
in the role of Supergirl, it's now apparent

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.940
that her performance has actually been even
better than she's been given credit for.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:24.730
If you've ever tried to play it off as if
you're not extremely uncomfortable while freezing

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:27.460
your tail off, you know that it's darn near
impossible.

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:31.740
For that matter, kudos to the cast of the
rest of the Arrowverse series, which also

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:35.520
shoot in Vancouver during those months when
the weather will pretty much kill you if you're

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:36.680
exposed to it for too long.

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:40.740
They, however, have at least gotten to wear
pants for the duration of their shows' runs.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:45.780
In addition to Kara's new look, Supergirl
season 5 will also feature a decidedly distinct

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:50.869
aesthetic from season 4, which saw the Girl
of Steel thwarting Luthor's plans to sow discord

00:01:50.869 --> 00:01:53.420
between the human and alien populations of
Earth.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:57.560
The season carried some obvious political
overtones, and while the themes explored in

00:01:57.580 --> 00:02:01.120
season 5 will be much different, they will
just as topical.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:05.380
Comic-Con fans were treated to a special preview
of the new batch of episodes which will deal

00:02:05.399 --> 00:02:10.300
with society's deepening reliance on technology,
with executive producer Robert Rovner going

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:13.380
so far as to call it the show's "Black Mirror
season."

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:17.840
Kara will also have to deal with the wrath
of her friend - and Lex Luthor's sister - Lena,

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:22.780
who was pretty unhappy to discover that Kara
had been hiding her secret identity from her

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:24.420
for their entire relationship.

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:29.200
The trailer also confirmed that, Lex Luthor,
who had been shot and left for dead by Lena,

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.980
was indeed rescued from his fate by the Monitor.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:34.420
He'll be back to menace our hero in the new
season.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:38.660
Season 5 has also added a few interesting
supporting characters, including Veronica

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:44.120
Mars' Julie Gonzalo as Andrea Rojas, a businesswoman
with super-heroic aspirations.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:48.720
Joining her will be Game of Thrones' Staz
Nair as William Dey, a hard-boiled reporter

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:50.870
hiding his connections to the criminal underworld.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:56.060
Finally, Being Human's Meghan Rath will portray
a female Brainiac 5, joining her real-life

00:02:56.060 --> 00:03:00.200
brother, Jesse Rath, who portrayed a male
Brainiac 5 in previous seasons.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:05.160
We'll see how all of the intrigue and interdimensional
weirdness plays out, as well as how Supergirl

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:10.270
season 5 might connect to the big Crisis on
Infinite Earths crossover slated for this

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:14.180
winter, when the new episodes begin airing
on The CW on October 6.

